On VS Code 

Terminal Commands to Start:
1. Compile the code: g++ main.cpp MedicineBatch.cpp -o pharmacy
2. Run the program: ./pharmacy

Live Demonstration Script (FEFO Logic)

1. Add the Inventory (Option 1)
Add these three batches exactly as shown to prove the system sorts them by expiration date, not by the order they were added.
Type 1 -> Paracetamol B-101 50 12 2027
Type 1 -> Paracetamol B-102 100 05 2027 (This expires first)
Type 1 -> Paracetamol B-103 30 01 2028 (This expires last)

2. Verify Sorting (Option 3)
Type 3 to view the stock.
Point out to your evaluator that B-102 is at the very top of the list because it expires first (May 2027), automatically applying the First-Expire-First-Out rule.

3. Demonstrate the Auto-Issue (Option 2)
Type 2 and issue 120 pills: Paracetamol 120
The terminal will show it pulling exactly 100 from B-102 (emptying the oldest batch) and the remaining 20 from B-101.

4. Final Proof (Option 3)
Type 3 to view the stock one last time.
Show that B-102 has been completely removed from the system and B-101 now only has 30 pills left.

5. Type 4 to exit 

